From: Notebook OS <notebookos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ppd-cache: find pwg-raster-document-resolution-supported

_ppdCreateFromIPP2() decides whether a printer can be driven as an IPP
Everywhere raster device with:

    is_pwg = ippContainsString(attr, "image/pwg-raster") && !is_apple &&
             (ippFindAttribute(supported,
                 "pwg-raster-document-resolution-supported",
                 IPP_TAG_KEYWORD) != NULL) && ...

but that attribute is 1setOf resolution (PWG 5102.4), not 1setOf keyword, so a
printer that reports it correctly is never found and is_pwg is never true. The
sibling lookup for pwg-raster-document-type-supported IS keyword and is right.

A printer that speaks PWG Raster but neither PDF nor Apple URF — an IPP
Everywhere device that is not AirPrint certified — therefore falls through to

    if (!is_apple && !is_pdf && !is_pwg)
      goto bad_ppd;

and no PPD can be generated for it at all, so it cannot be set up driverless
even though it is exactly the class of printer IPP Everywhere was defined for.

Match on the attribute's presence rather than a wrong tag, which also tolerates
printers that send it as a keyword.

Signed-off-by: Notebook OS <notebookos@localhost>
---
 cups/ppd-cache.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cups/ppd-cache.c b/cups/ppd-cache.c
@@ -3544,7 +3544,7 @@
     is_apple = ippContainsString(attr, "image/urf") && (ippFindAttribute(supported, "urf-supported", IPP_TAG_KEYWORD) != NULL);
     is_pdf   = ippContainsString(attr, "application/pdf");
     is_pwg   = ippContainsString(attr, "image/pwg-raster") && !is_apple &&
-	       (ippFindAttribute(supported, "pwg-raster-document-resolution-supported", IPP_TAG_KEYWORD) != NULL) &&
+	       (ippFindAttribute(supported, "pwg-raster-document-resolution-supported", IPP_TAG_ZERO) != NULL) &&
 	       (ippFindAttribute(supported, "pwg-raster-document-type-supported", IPP_TAG_KEYWORD) != NULL);
 
     if (ippContainsString(attr, "image/jpeg"))
